{"id":"mimid-1wgh.99","title":"JMAP: jmap-chat-push: content pushes a phone can render","description":"In scope by decision mimid-1wgh.98 (Mark, 2026-11-22). Not planned: read the draft, face the tension below, and put a plan in this field for Mark before any code.

WHAT THE DRAFT DOES. Reverses mimid-1wgh.12.30 (no PushSubscription) for this draft. chatPush delivers a ChatMessagePush with message metadata and an optional body snippet so a phone renders a notification with no follow-up request.

THE TENSION, to settle first: mimid's provider holds ciphertext and cannot produce a body snippet. The agent holds plaintext and already does exactly this for IRC over soju.im/webpush (crates/mimid-agent-irc/src/webpush.rs, RFC 8291 encryption to the client's keys, RFC 8292 VAPID). So the likely shape is the AGENT serving chatPush to its local clients, with the provider serving metadata-only pushes at most. Read the draft against what an E2EE deployment can honestly send, and report to Mark whether the draft needs a paragraph saying so.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.068401626Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.068401626Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mimid-1wgh.99","depends_on_id":"mimid-1wgh","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.097737965Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}

